 # RivalRadar
-RivalRadar OSRS plugin+
+RivalRadar is a RuneLite external plugin scaffold for tracking a configured Old School RuneScape rival and preparing XP comparison checks against public Wise Old Man data.
+
+The current implementation is intentionally lightweight and ready for manual RuneLite testing: it loads as `RivalRadar`, displays a small overlay with the configured rival/skill, and sends a login chat message so plugin startup can be verified quickly in developer mode.
+
+## Features
+
+- RuneLite plugin metadata wired to `com.itmeansbigmountain.rivalradar.RivalRadarPlugin`.
+- Configurable status overlay for manual smoke testing.
+- Configurable rival name and comparison skill fields.
+- Public Wise Old Man helper methods for player and hiscore requests.
+- Unit tests for default config values, overlay formatting, and Wise Old Man URL construction.
+
+## Configuration
+
+RuneLite settings group: `rivalradar`
+
+| Setting | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Show overlay | `true` | Toggles the RivalRadar overlay panel. |
+| Rival name | blank | OSRS username to compare against during testing. |
+| Comparison skill | `overall` | Skill used for planned XP comparison lookups. |
+| Welcome message | `tracking enabled` | Login chat message emitted by the plugin. |
+
+## API usage notes
+
+`WOMApiHelper` targets public Wise Old Man endpoints under `https://api.wiseoldman.net/v1` and does not require credentials. Keep any future live polling off the game thread, cache responses, and respect Wise Old Man rate limits before expanding the plugin from manual-test status to production comparison logic.
+
+## Build and test
+
+Use Java 11 for RuneLite compatibility:
+
+```bash
+export JAVA_HOME=/opt/data/jdks/current-java11
+./gradlew test --no-daemon -q
+./gradlew assemble --no-daemon -q
+```
+
+To launch RuneLite in developer mode from this repo:
+
+```bash
+export JAVA_HOME=/opt/data/jdks/current-java11
+./gradlew run --no-daemon
+```
+
+## Manual RuneLite testing checklist
+
+1. Start the plugin with `./gradlew run --no-daemon`.
+2. Confirm RuneLite launches in developer mode and lists `RivalRadar` as a loaded external plugin.
+3. Log into a test account and confirm the chat box shows `RivalRadar: tracking enabled`.
+4. Open the RivalRadar config, set a rival name and skill, and confirm the overlay updates.
+5. Toggle `Show overlay` off/on and confirm the panel hides and returns without errors.
+6. Watch the RuneLite logs for startup, shutdown, or API-related exceptions.
+
+## Plugin Hub prep notes
+
+Before submitting to the RuneLite Plugin Hub, replace this manual-test scaffold with the final comparison UX, add screenshots/GIFs, verify all live API calls are cached/backgrounded, and confirm the support URL points to the published repository.
